                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Keyboard & Mouse[/h1]\n[i] Note: If you're on the Oculus Rift, you have to follow these instructions:\n1. Do a Windows 7 compatibility fix on file executable JonahsPath_VIVE and save\n2. Run Steam VR\n3. Double click on file executable JonahsPath_Vive\n4. Make sure that under the Game Properties General Tab on Steam that the option Use Desktop Game Theatre while SteamVR is active option is turned off / not checked.[/i]\n\nThis is about a 6 minute purely cinematic submarine ride on what looks like an alien water world at nighttime. It's not as good as the submarine ride on Summer Funland. However, it's still pretty nice. The scales seem to be off a bit, but it doesn't detract from the experience. I enjoyed the visuals. It is a slow speed ride, so it's mostly about enjoying the surroundings although there is a climatic ending in keeping with the name of the title.\n\n[b]Rate 6/10. You can also watch my video of the complete thing here: https://youtu.be/1CkOHWgO-b4 [/b]",
